=== END ===

The only compile error was in `kernel.d.ts`. `Ledger extends QuotaStore`, and both interfaces declared a `read` method with incompatible signatures:

- `QuotaStore.read(account)` returned quota state.
- `Ledger.read(query)` iterated ledger events.

The fix renames the quota accessor to `QuotaStore.quota(account)`, which no longer clashes with any `Ledger` method. The design is unchanged:

- Quota state still has its own interface, so it can be shared across harnesses (scenario 7).
- A ledger may still serve as the quota backend by implementing both interfaces.

No scenario reads the quota store directly, so nothing else changes.

